# scenarios/4_intellectual_work.books: loaded by ledger_server into 4_intellectual_work.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	4. Intellectual work: hours billed, hours capitalised
about	Hours never enter the books, only the salaries paid for them (Wages and salaries). Work billed to a client is a cost this year, against the sale it brings.
about	Work that builds something lasting, here the company's software, is capitalised: Own work capitalised takes its cost out of the year's costs and Software holds it as an asset, which then loses value to depreciation over its life.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Share capital
account	550000	asset	Bank
account	620000	expense	Wages and salaries
account	400000	asset	Trade receivables
account	700000	revenue	Sales
account	720000	revenue	Own work capitalised
account	211000	asset	Software
account	630000	expense	Depreciation
entry	2011-01-02	The founder puts in savings
posting	Share capital	-1000000
posting	Bank	1000000
entry	2011-04-30	An employee's salary for April, spent building the company's software
posting	Bank	-200000
posting	Wages and salaries	200000
entry	2011-04-30	The software is capitalised: the work becomes an asset
posting	Own work capitalised	-200000
posting	Software	200000
entry	2011-05-31	Salary for May, spent on a client's project
posting	Bank	-300000
posting	Wages and salaries	300000
entry	2011-05-31	The client's project is invoiced to a customer for 4,000
posting	Sales	-400000
posting	Trade receivables	400000
entry	2011-06-30	The customer pays
posting	Trade receivables	-400000
posting	Bank	400000
entry	2011-12-31	The software loses a quarter of its value to depreciation
posting	Software	-50000
posting	Depreciation	50000
